    {
      "text": "So, these are citations from across every system that it's connected to. I can follow them back if I need more details, but that helps me know that it didn't hallucinate the important parts.",
      "timestamp_sec": 659,
      "why": "Names citation traceability as the verification mechanism for AI-compiled documentation."
    },
    {
      "text": "And the librarian has access to documentation and the library of knowledge items about your company and the schema of prior failed queries. And so it basically gives your agent a just-in-time memory of all the important things.",
      "timestamp_sec": 760,
      "why": "The clearest definition of the librarian pattern, including the prior-failed-queries input."
    },
    {
      "text": "They are going to spin up a team of independent analysts who all look at the data independently and come up with an evidence-cited opinion for what they think the attribution credit of that deal should be.",
      "timestamp_sec": 840,
      "why": "Defines the jury half of the jury-and-judge workflow."
    },
    {
      "text": "I'm treating them as input, and I'm going to weigh the reasoning quality of each of these analysts, and then I'm going to help you come up with the final version here. And if there's not enough consensus, then I'll escalate and expand the jury.",
      "timestamp_sec": 877,
      "why": "Specifies how the judge aggregates — reasoning quality, not majority vote — plus the escalation rule."
    },
    {
      "text": "Turns out multiple researchers with somebody who helps at the end is better than a single person kind of perseverating on that forever.",
      "timestamp_sec": 877,
      "why": "The human-analogy justification for multi-agent research over a single long-running agent."
    },
    {
      "text": "In my experience, you can't fix stupid. So, this basically means friends don't let friends use really bad harnesses or low intelligent models for important work.",
      "timestamp_sec": 911,
      "why": "The agent-tiers thesis, bluntly stated."
    },
    {
      "text": "any AI product where it's been crowbarred into a pre- subscription model is probably not something that you should be using for anything important because the margin on those plans just doesn't leave enough space for an intelligent reasoning model to work",
      "timestamp_sec": 911,
      "why": "An economic mechanism for why cheap embedded AI features underperform."
    },
    {
      "text": "You need it to have attributes like sub agents, plan mode, full MCP support. It should be able to use file editing",
      "timestamp_sec": 972,
